<title>SOUTH KOREA: Tong Kook to buy back 100,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Tong Kook to buy back 100,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Tong Kook Spinning Co said on Thursday it would buy back its own 100,000 common shares from June 2 to September 1.</p>
<p>The buy-back, representing 2.5 percent of the company's total outstanding shares, was aimed at boosting share prices. Tong Kook shed 90 won to 5,200 at 0210 GMT on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
